# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Docker build context exclusions
#
# The builder stage runs `COPY . .`, so anything not excluded here is copied
# into the image. Three of these matter more than the rest:
#
#   node_modules  The deps stage installs Linux binaries with `npm ci`. Copying
#                 the host tree over the top replaces them with whatever the
#                 developer's machine produced — on Windows or macOS that means
#                 native modules for the wrong platform.
#
#   .data         The file-store fallback writes real benchmark submissions
#                 here. Next.js traces the file into `.next/standalone/.data/`
#                 at build time, and the runtime stage copies that directory
#                 wholesale, so local rows would ship inside the image and be
#                 served as public benchmark statistics on first boot.
#
#   .env*         Never let a local secret become an image layer.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Dependencies and build output — regenerated inside the image
node_modules
.next
out

# Local persistence. See note above: this must never reach the image.
.data

# Version control and CI definitions
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Test, coverage and report artefacts
coverage
e2e-results
playwright-report
tests
playwright.config.ts
vitest.config.ts

# Local environment and editor state
.env
.env.*
.vscode
.idea
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Infrastructure and documentation — not needed by the running server
infra
azuredeploy.json
createUiDefinition.json
azure.yaml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
*.md

# Incremental TypeScript state
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
